Subject: [PATCH] wifi: Do not reinit BCM43752 firmware on RX FIFO overflow

The 101.10.591 driver enables FW_REINIT_RXF0OVFL for BCM43752. Under
sustained receive load it then sends WLC_INIT about once per second. The
CE firmware 18.35.387.11 traps after five reinits within 10000 s
("Frequent re-inits leading to TRAP!"). The driver then raises HANG and
powers WLAN off, and nothing on CE turns WLAN on again. The box stays
offline until a power cycle, and playback over the network freezes.

Without the reinit, the receive path keeps running at full rate under
the same load. Keep the other BCM43752 workarounds.

--- a/bcmdhd.101.10.591.x/dhd_config.c
+++ b/bcmdhd.101.10.591.x/dhd_config.c
@@ -6187,8 +6187,10 @@
 	conf->in4way |= STA_REASSOC_RETRY;
 #endif
 	if (conf->chip == BCM43752_CHIP_ID)
-		conf->war = SET_CHAN_INCONN | FW_REINIT_INCSA | FW_REINIT_EMPTY_SCAN |
-			FW_REINIT_RXF0OVFL;
+		/* No FW_REINIT_RXF0OVFL: the CE 18.35.387.11 firmware traps after five
+		 * host reinits within 10000 s, and nothing on CE restarts WLAN after a trap.
+		 */
+		conf->war = SET_CHAN_INCONN | FW_REINIT_INCSA | FW_REINIT_EMPTY_SCAN;
 	else if (conf->chip == BCM43711_CHIP_ID || conf->chip == BCM4612_CHIP_ID)
 		conf->war = SET_CHAN_INCONN;
 	else
